WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
It's one of, this is one of the reasons I recovered from it.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.760
And by the way, it's much better to not have TDS.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.760
I'm happier, I'm healthier, more successful.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.720
I even think I got a little more attractive

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.720
after I got rid of my Trump derangement syndrome, yes.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.760
You know, I watched, I'm a reporter in Seattle,

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.459
and frankly, I could not care any less

00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:21.459
what any of you have to say about this meeting.

00:00:21.459 --> 00:00:22.480
Could not care any less.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.320
We're not here for you.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.040
I'm not here to convince any of you

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.540
that Antifa is a real thing,

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.660
because if you have not come to that conclusion by now,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.440
you are never gonna come to that conclusion

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.160
because you don't wanna see it.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.400
And you're gonna go and you're gonna say

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.959
it's a bunch of right-wing conservative influencers

00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:38.680
who are here spinning a tale.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.560
I was one of you.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.560
I was a mainstream reporter in Seattle for 10 years.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.639
I was a TV reporter on the streets doing my job,

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:50.279
and I was still assaulted by Antifa.

00:00:50.279 --> 00:00:51.919
So it's not about being conservative.

00:00:51.919 --> 00:00:55.160
It's about people who go there and show what they're doing.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.840
And when I saw after all those years

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.220
that the media wouldn't be honest about what was happening,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.299
that Democratic politicians wouldn't be honest

00:01:02.299 --> 00:01:04.500
about what was happening, I thought, well, gosh,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.820
if they're not being honest about that,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.260
maybe they're not being honest about President Trump either.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.099
And it opened my mind to just looking at things

00:01:11.099 --> 00:01:11.980
for what they were.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.620
And now I find you quite funny, actually.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.820
Now I'm, it's like I said, I'm much happier about it.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.540
But for me, again, I could not care any less

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.220
the stories that they go to print.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.220
This is what I care about.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.180
We have three and a half years.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.580
Nothing is guaranteed,

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.139
although I think if Democrats keep it up,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.720
we'll probably have Republican presidents

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.160
for the next three decades.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.279
But nothing is guaranteed.

00:01:31.279 --> 00:01:34.000
And so what I want to see over the next three and a half years

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.900
is a full court press to dismantle Antifa once and for all

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:38.919
in a meaningful way.

00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:41.940
I know, Andy, we talked before this about some ideas.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.040
That's really what we want to,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.360
I don't care what the media says.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.279
I don't care what Democrats say.

00:01:46.279 --> 00:01:48.400
They will never wake up to this fact.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.699
So we want the federal government

00:01:49.699 --> 00:01:52.180
to take as many of these cases as possible.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.160
Look at the interstate travel between Portland and Seattle

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.860
when it comes to these people

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.820
who are committing violent acts.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.820
And hopefully in three and a half years,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.940
they will be a shell of their former selves.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.620
And it's Antifa and many others, unfortunately.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.020
There are many others, bad ones.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.779
Most have been named terrorist organizations.

00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:14.860
There are a couple that we're going to,

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.619
but I think we've got it pretty well covered.

00:02:16.619 --> 00:02:17.619
But there are many others,

00:02:17.619 --> 00:02:21.899
but very specifically today's Antifa, and it's really bad.

00:02:21.899 --> 00:02:24.020
And we're going to get it cleaned up.

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:24.880
Andy, did you have something?

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.720
Thank you very much.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.720
I'm glad you no longer have TDS.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.119
I feel very good about that.

00:02:30.199 --> 00:02:31.559
Thank you.

00:02:31.559 --> 00:02:34.039
Thank you, Mr. President and members of the cabinet.

00:02:34.039 --> 00:02:35.220
I have a lot of gratitude

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.080
and a little bit about my background.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.520
I'm born in Portland, Oregon from there.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:44.000
And growing up, it's always been left-wing, very progressive

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.940
and I liked it.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.839
It had cafes and artists

00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:49.600
and those who lived a bohemian lifestyle.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.679
And in 2016, I was a graduate student at Portland State

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.059
studying political science.

00:02:55.059 --> 00:02:56.820
I was an editor at the student paper there,

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.059
a very progressive paper.

00:02:58.059 --> 00:02:59.979
And I was assigned to cover

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.860
the election night demonstrations.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.339
Well, the elections night protests turned to riots,

00:03:07.339 --> 00:03:09.779
three days of violent rioting in Portland.

00:03:09.779 --> 00:03:14.179
And it was the first time that I saw groups dressed in black

00:03:14.179 --> 00:03:15.339
with their faces covered.

00:03:15.339 --> 00:03:17.779
This was four years before COVID.

00:03:17.779 --> 00:03:21.020
Some of them were waving the black flag of anarchism,

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.960
some the red flag of Marxism.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.679
And within seconds, they would ravage one street

00:03:26.679 --> 00:03:29.160
to another, to another, to another.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.320
And the next day I would read the legacy media,

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.020
which I still read at that time and looked forward to,

00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:37.399
and I looked up to those journalists.

00:03:37.399 --> 00:03:41.479
And I was really shocked to see that the narrative

00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:44.839
was that these, in my view,

00:03:44.839 --> 00:03:48.279
anti-democratic political violence

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:53.300
was legitimate acts of protest because people were,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.940
they were concerned about racism or all these other lies.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.699
And so for the next four years,

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:03.660
I just continued going out with my video camera.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.940
I thought, look, people can ignore what I write

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.899
because of spin, but videos can quite speak for themselves.

00:04:10.899 --> 00:04:15.899
And in 2019, it led to me nearly losing my life.

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:21.480
I was covering another Antifa protest turn riot,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.720
at that point had been routine in Portland.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.600
And then I was ambushed in a mob beating

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.519
and I had never been in a fight.

00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:32.839
I didn't even realize that I was being assaulted

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.119
until seconds in.

00:04:35.119 --> 00:04:39.079
And the punches came from everywhere on my head and my face.

00:04:39.079 --> 00:04:41.959
And I was bleeding out of my eyes and ears.

00:04:41.959 --> 00:04:44.480
And then they threw all the drinks in my eyes

00:04:44.779 --> 00:04:48.299
to humiliate me further and to laugh at me.

00:04:48.299 --> 00:04:52.579
And I was rushed to the hospital in a ambulance and CT scan.

00:04:52.579 --> 00:04:55.339
And I had subarachnoid hemorrhage,

00:04:55.339 --> 00:04:57.899
which is bleeding in the brain and nearly died.

00:04:57.899 --> 00:05:01.220
And after surviving that, the.

